Z||000008||Cheever3000||09-23-2001||10:58 AM||||I think everybody just had a busy Saturday.  <BR>The recent tragedy and its unfolding events have consumed our thoughts and maybe drained us a little.  <P>I'd like to assure you that a lot of preparation went into this club before the announcement was made.  This is not a fly-by-night half-hearted attempt, but a serious organization.  We realize that claiming to represent Fiero owners everywhere is a task not to be taken lightly.  For anything you need beyond your local club, this club will be there for you, to listen and actively respond to your expectations and ideas.  We're not just saying "here's a new club you should join", we know there must be a "why", and "what will it do for me".  There is much we want to accomplish, but it's important to hear it from <I>you</I>.  Give us some feedback.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||WKDFIRO||09-23-2001||11:55 AM||||This sounds very familiar to the organization that George had pitched to the Western Regional Presidents as a way to unify the FOCOA factions in San Leandro.<P>Is this an extension of those plans or something all together?||||reg||5
Z||000010||tgowens||09-23-2001||02:06 PM||||WKDFIRO, while there may be similarities, this is altogether something entirely new. What George was speaking about earlier did not come to pass due to the fact that that group cannot and will not embrace change. It is now, as it has been and always will be. That was the reasoning behind creating Classic Fiero Owners Group International. We felt, after attending their national show, that nothing was going to change, that the complaints that were being voiced by their members were not being addressed, and that it was time to create a faction that would listen, respond, and support the member......<P>This organization (CFOG-I) has committed itself to acessability and accountability to its members with response and resolution....not to repeat the mistakes of previous organizations of its type but to enhance the value of the organization to its members.<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||BOILERMAKER||09-23-2001||10:09 PM||||I'm already a member too.  I can't wait to see what this club has to offer to its members and the fiero community.||||reg||1
Z||000012||artherd||09-24-2001||05:19 AM||||Hi everyone, I'm also a member (and it turns out, on the board  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>This club is set to offer a whole lot, from local 'start a club in your neighborhood' kits, to a group auto insurance program (....... YES!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  to an 800-line 'fiero help' line you can call when you're *under* your car and are wondering where the heck this little bolt-ish thing goes, or which way that steering rack went anyway.<P>CFOG-I will also be incorpoated as a non-profit full company, and is an independant entity.  It will also publish full financial statements on a regular basis to *all* members.   Although many buisnesses and individuals are donating both time and materials that are assisting the club (thanks guys!) they remain seperate donating parties, and must for example still buy ad space, pay for membership, etc.<P>We're not out to replace or undermine any existing orginazations, and infact all clubs can join the global  CFOG-I orginazation for no more than it costs one person.  Any and all Fiero people are welcome, this is about the cars, and it's going to be fun!<P>This global-level club is geared towards encouraging and supporting local clubs as integral parts of each other, the end goal to ALL of this of course is for us all to ENJOY OUR CARS!!!<P>That's why we're here, and I personally think this club is going to be a great way to get together and meet new Fiero people, and just have a great time driving!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000013||AusFiero||09-24-2001||06:00 AM||||Australian Director here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Even recruited my first new Aussie member tonight. Now just have to get my act together to pay my dues. That's what I get for being away for the weekend see. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||14
Z||000014||Boomtastic||09-24-2001||08:52 AM||||The personnel roster reads like a "Who's Who" in the Fiero community, and if that doesn't get you excited nothing will! I'm proud to be affiliated with CFOG-I, and foresee great things for the future.<P>EDIT: Crap - was I supposed to say I am the Regional Director for the Northeast?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Boomtastic (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000015||stimpy||09-24-2001||09:15 AM||||I am proud to see this gaining strength and momentum. As the regional director for the south central region (Louisiana, Oklahoma, Texas, and Arkansas) I see bright days ahead. I do need to get some help. If there are any forum members in LA, TX, or AR, I do need deputy directors. PLEASE, do not hesitate to make your presence known. This is all about making some waves, and to do that, we need fresh people with fresh ideas. Holler at me, and I'll be sure to holler back.||||reg||1
Z||000016||fieroshop||09-24-2001||12:38 PM||||I persanally would like to see comments about this topic......<P>Terry and I will be leavung here and driving to Kentuckey at noon today and I will be back here on Monday of next week....<P>We will see some of you along the way.<P><BR>------------------<BR> <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Songman||09-24-2001||01:01 PM||||Even though I am not a poster on this forum anymore, I am still very active in the Fiero community and was very excited when I first talked to Terry about helping to get things going. I think without a doubt that this group can be the biggest thing I have found to help me with my Fiero since I first found this forum.<P>I am very happy to be the Regional Director for my area, and even happier to have Doug Kinney as a Deputy Director. Of course, the Tennessee Fiero Owners group will be an affiliated club and I hope all of the members will take advantage of the benefits of this international group. This reminds me very much of the Corvette group I have belonged to in the past. <P>Now I will slide back into the shadows but invite anyone from the states of Maryland, Virginia, North Carolina, Kentucky, Tennessee, West Virginia, Delaware, or Washington DC to get in touch with me if I can answer any questions for you.<P>dalehouston@home.com||||reg||7
Z||000018||fieroshop||10-01-2001||07:01 PM||||Well back here at home on the West coast after travelling across country to Ohio. <BR>It was a good trip and I met with some very nice Fiero People.<BR>The last night I was in Ohio Terry and I got together with some new found friends and we discussed the club and had a few more Fiero Owners join our organization.<BR>This club cannot and will not function if we have no members. <BR>Come on guys sign-up and be counted. Get involved and we can make this the best club in the world.<BR>Yes we are there to support the Fiero and their owners.<BR>Go the the membership page and fill out your application and let's get this club on a roll. <BR>All of us on the board promise that you will have support and Fiero Comraderie. We will also have our own shows, a technical toll free hotline you can call. As I am writing this message as the president of CFOG International, there are several insurance companies that I am speaking to about a club insurance for our beloved Fiero's. Al of this cannot happen if we do not have participation.<BR>Please, sign-up today so that we may be able to get and do all of the things we are trying to do.<P><BR>George I. Miller<BR>Classic Fiero Owners Group International. <P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000019||Cheever3000||10-01-2001||09:35 PM||||The biggest thing I see that this can accomplish is <B>unity</B>.  Right now the Fiero community is divided.  This is not the time to blame anyone for it, this is the time to do something about it and get our passion focused.  We need to be available for the new Fiero owner, and for those considering ownership.  We need to give veteran owners a sense of belonging to the family of all Fiero owners everywhere.  We need to <B>share</B> resources, talents, ideas and more between the local clubs & individuals so nobody is reinventing the wheel (no pun intended).  We need to take our rightful place of respect among the automotive world, with a singular voice which proudly represents all of us.  Without a strong unifying body our fractioned efforts do no more than satisfy a few people in widespread places for a short time.  We're talking about a bonfire of hope, compared to a flickering flame.  Let's turn that twinkle in the eye of every Fieroholic into a realized dream.  Let's turn our desperation into determination.  Give your enthusiasm a tuneup, and be part of a family running smoothly on all cylinders.  There's just one way to do this right, and that's <B>togetherness</B>.  We Fiero owners all need each other.  That's all CFOG-I is here for.  Nobody's looking to make a buck from your dues - it's a non-profit organization with open books.  It's put together and running for <B>YOU</B>, it will answer to <B>YOU</B>, and it will succeed only because of <B>YOU</B>!  <P>Do you want unity?<BR>Do you want representation?<BR>Join us.  <P>Read the website.  Email the officers & directors with your questions.  Talk it over with your local club or the Fiero people you hang out with.  Do you have specific needs or ideas, prerequisites - priorities which must be met before you will join? Let us know!  There's much we want to do, and we're just getting started.  As this movement keeps rolling, we can do much, with YOUR involvement.  We need you, your Fiero family needs you, and you need something to put the whole package together.  <P>This club has the best chance ever for success.  Be part of that success.  We can't afford the alternative.<P><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I><BR>Vice President, <A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000020||87ECO5||10-01-2001||11:42 PM||||Enjoyed finally meeting George, seeing Terry again, and meeting his lovely daughter Nicole.  Had a few laughs, a few too many drinks, and discussed some good information regarding the club.<P>CFOG-I will be a tremendous asset to the Fiero community.  I look forward to taking part in this effort.||||reg||14
Z||000021||MinnGreenGT||10-02-2001||12:02 AM||||George & Terry... too bad you guys didn't make it through this territory- would be nice to meet you guys in person!<P>As a deputy director for the upper midwest area, I'm hoping to see a surge in growth of this club over the next few months to a year.  Like many others have said, we need to stick together to make the Fiero community a tightly-knit group.  I hope that many will review the info on the <A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank> website </A> and seriously consider and commit to making this organization work!  <P>If you're still spending your membership fee at another national club and aren't satisfied with what you're getting... why not take a chance and try out CFOG-I?  If you still aren't satisfied with the club after your first year's membership- then by all means you are still free to go back to the previous club!  We really need everyone to help make this work. ||||reg||1
Z||000022||fieroshop||10-02-2001||03:01 PM||||Something that might be of interest to all of you at this time is we as the board decided to reduce membership in the month of October to $25.00.<BR>The reason for this, is that some clubs have not yet voted to join and if you join and are not affiliated with a club, dues would be $40.00.<BR>So we are giving everybody the incentive to join at affiliated club price.<BR>So what are you waiting for!!!! Sign-up now and save.<BR>Remember, this club is for you and run by the membership.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 10-02-2001).]||||reg||6
